 "notes": [
  "Trained on 1,467 real ethereum addresses: 599 deposit addresses and 868 others. The model reads what an address does (forwarding, timing, who pays its fees), never a label. The deposit addresses are the ones a block explorer tagged, a truth our rules never saw.",
  "By time (latest 294 addresses by first transfer, unseen): PR-AUC 0.9547, Brier 0.0574, ECE 0.0563, precision 0.803 and recall 0.9815 at 0.5. The rule \"forwards 90% or more to one wallet\" alone gives precision 0.5545 and recall 0.5648 on the same addresses: that, not chance, is the bar.",
  "By exchange: each exchange's addresses (1,196 in total) were scored by a model that never saw that exchange. Pooled PR-AUC 0.7615, recall 0.1002 and precision 0.9091 at 0.5. With 2 exchanges, each of those models learned deposit addresses from one exchange only, and what it learned did not carry over.",
  "Cross-fit: each address is scored by a model that never trained on it but knows its exchange from the exchange's other addresses. On all 1,467 addresses: PR-AUC 0.9504, Brier 0.0607, ECE 0.028. Most of those models also trained on later addresses, so this describes the scores; it is not an accuracy to expect on new addresses.",
  "Probabilities are calibrated with Venn-Abers on addresses the trees did not train on, at this dataset's class mix (the negatives are a capped sample), not at the mix of the chain at large.",
  "The hard case, by time: of the 49 other wallets that also forward 90% or more of what they receive to one wallet, the model still calls 15 a deposit address (1 of 49 by exchange, 37 of 204 cross-fit).",
  "597 of the 868 others are wallets that paid into the deposit addresses; the rest are labelled wallets that are not deposit addresses. A wallet that never dealt with an exchange is not in this sample, so how often the model would take such a wallet for a deposit address is not measured here.",
  "The two features that read exchange labels were left out of the shipped model: with them it scores PR-AUC 0.9752 by time and recall 0.1569 on an exchange whose labels are hidden.",
  "This model scores no label. It is the benchmark against a truth the rules never saw; the labels carry the scores of the model trained on their own chain."
 ],
